  "cover_text": "Georgetown — Sally Long, a long-time resident of the Washington, D.C., community focused on increasing people’s connections to topical meaning, is a well-respected cultural engagement designer with Boston-based Design:Platform.\n\nMatthew Macnamara, design manager for Design:Platform, said: “Sally’s creativity, attention to detail, and passion for wider cultural engagement lead her to enjoy immersion in the local context of D.C. and the Washington, D.C., community.”\n\nLong was part of the community leadership group involved in the consortium for the artist and designer shown above, a group founded by the Political Economy Research Fund and led by Garrett Brockington in 2014.\n\nD",
